# READING:
# - Same B*S (8192 tok/step) and same memory (40.1G) as the S1024/B8 run, but
#   MFU HALVED (40.3% -> 21.8%). Two causes:
#   (1) _WindowedAttnMixer.forward hands SDPA a dense S x S bool mask ->
#       arbitrary-mask SDPA computes FULL quadratic attention then masks.
#       S^2 waste grows 16x from S1024 to S4096 while useful (banded) work
#       grows 4x. The architecture is linear-in-S; this implementation is not.
#   (2) B=2 underutilizes SMs on batch-parallel kernels (scan, elementwise).
# - FIX (queued): FlexAttention (torch>=2.5) sliding-window BlockMask does
#   only the banded work at near-flash speed — contained change to the mixer's
#   forward; step() decode path unaffected. Re-measure S4096 after.
# - Implication for the long-context question: big-VRAM cards (B200 180G) buy
#   the MEMORY for long-S training (~8x the B*S budget vs 80G), but until the
#   flex fix lands, ~half the throughput is given back at S4096. Software
#   first, then buy context.
